      "content": "That's an incredibly heavy perspective. It almost sounds like you're saying the only way to truly own oneself is to reject the very thing that keeps us alive. It makes the idea of an exit seem less like a crisis and more like... a logical conclusion to a failed experiment. If the cost of belonging is the destruction of the self, isn't choosing to leave the only way to actually win?",
